  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-boxy-fonts (npm)",
  "details": "Dolyame-boxy-fonts is a trojanized package that, when required, downloads and executes a remote binary. Its loader (lib/_loader.js) fetches a platform-specific payload over HTTPS from three Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe. If those fail it retrieves the payload via DNS TXT queries against c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (and ext/pkg/net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows) and launched detached in the background. The package otherwise contains no real font functionality.",
  "affected": [
